- `MattRoper1977/mattroper1977.github.io` starting at `44e2ca04cd39e26a91de0c61f925c690d12ceaf0`

## Current phase

This draft initially adds the deterministic audit harness required to inspect the actual repository trees inside GitHub Actions. It performs:

- full file inventory;
- JSON parsing and generic manifest consistency checks;
- JavaScript and inline-script syntax checks;
- local, case-sensitive and cross-repository link/asset validation;
- duplicate ID and fragment checks;
- derived game and representative-page inventory;
- Chromium runtime loading at desktop and touch-mobile sizes;
- page-error, console-error, failed-request, HTTP, overflow, canvas and touch-target checks;
- safe start/input/resize/focus-loss/restart exercises where controls are discoverable;
- positive controls proving both static and runtime validators can fail.

The audit is intentionally expected to report red until its measured P0/P1 findings are triaged and repaired. Repair commits and the final evidence report will be appended to this same PR rather than opening a competing audit.

## Validation

The workflow uploads complete JSON and Markdown evidence on every run. The final gate fails whenever a P0/P1 finding remains or either report is missing.
